    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `timezone` field flows from the same region-and-hash identity that already backs `locality`.\n\n1. **`Timezone.java`** (new function class, `rest/function/owner/`) \u2014 a pinned region-to-timezone lookup: `NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney`, `VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne`, `QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane`; returns `null` for `UNKNOWN` or any unlisted region.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `timezone` mapping that derives the region via the existing `Locality.ofCustomerCode(owner.getCustomerCode())` and feeds it to `Timezone.of(...)`, so timezone comes from the same locality/region the DTO already exposes.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `timezone` string property to the `OwnerDto` schema (so the generated DTO has the field).\n\nThe acceptance test `coreReturnsTimezoneForRegion` (Sydney/postcode 2000 \u2192 NSW \u2192 `Australia/Sydney`) passes, and no existing test regressed.",
